def make(i,prompt,opts,ans,exp,strat,steps,diff): return {"id":f"question-english-performance-3-{i}","subject":"english","type":"single-choice","prompt":prompt,"options":[{"id":k,"text":v} for k,v in opts.items()],"knowledgeIds":[KG],"difficulty":diff,"answer":{"value":ans,"explanation":exp},"provenance":{"origin":"original","license":"All rights reserved","sourceUrl":SOURCES[0]["url"],"sourceLocator":"三份公開英文試題僅供能力方向研究；未複製原題、選項、文章或答案。","authoringNote":"依官方課綱 KG 與公開英文試題的英文閱讀理解能力方向獨立編寫；待第二輪 AI／Terra 內容複核。"},"reviewStatus":"draft","updatedAt":"2026-09-09","lessonId":LESSON,"examPatternRefs":refs(),"solutionStrategy":strat,"solutionSteps":steps}
Q=[
make(1,"Read: 'Every Friday, our class places leftover fruit in a basket by the office. Families can take it after school, so less food is thrown away.' What is the main idea?",{"A":"The class shares extra fruit to reduce food waste.","B":"The office sells fruit every morning.","C":"Families must bring food to school on Friday.","D":"The class has stopped eating fruit."},"A","The passage connects leftover fruit, family sharing, and less waste; A summarizes all three ideas.","Collect the repeated action and its stated result, then choose the option broad enough to include both.",["Identify the object: leftover fruit.","Identify the action: place it in a basket for families.","Read the result: less food is thrown away.","Reject claims about selling, required donations, or stopping fruit.","Choose A because it states the passage's purpose and result."],"easy"),
make(2,"Read: 'The school bus leaves at 7:10. Mia arrives at the stop at 7:00, but the bus is delayed by heavy rain and comes at 7:25.' When does the bus actually come?",{"A":"7:00","B":"7:10","C":"7:25","D":"7:35"},"C","The passage states that rain delays the bus and it comes at 7:25; 7:10 is the planned departure.","Separate the scheduled time from the actual event time signaled by delayed and comes.",["Locate the planned departure: 7:10.","Locate Mia's arrival: 7:00.","Find the actual arrival after the delay.","Match comes at with 7:25.","Choose C because it answers when the bus actually comes."],"easy"),
make(3,"Read: 'Leo moved his plant closer to the window because its leaves were turning pale. After two weeks, new green leaves appeared.' Why did Leo move the plant?",{"A":"He wanted to give it more light.","B":"He wanted to hide the pale leaves.","C":"He needed the window for a book.","D":"He planned to stop watering it."},"A","Because links the pale leaves to moving the plant closer to the window, which provides more light.","Use the because clause and the physical change in location to infer the purpose of the action.",["Find the action: moving the plant closer to the window.","Read the reason after because.","Connect a window with receiving more light.","Reject hiding, book space, and stopping water because they are not stated.","Select A because it explains the move and fits the later green leaves."],"medium"),
make(4,"Read: 'Nora found a wallet on the playground. She gave it to the office, where the staff could contact its owner.' What does She refer to?",{"A":"Nora","B":"the wallet","C":"the playground","D":"the office"},"A","The person who found the wallet and gave it to the office is Nora, so She refers to Nora.","Track the grammatical subject capable of performing the action gave it.",["List the people and objects in the first sentence.","Find the action in the second sentence: gave it.","Ask which item can perform that action.","Eliminate wallet, playground, and office because they cannot be the giver here.","Choose A because She continues the person Nora."],"easy"),
make(5,"Read: 'The first trail is shorter but steep. The second is longer and mostly flat. Our group chose the second trail because two members had sore knees.' Why did the group choose the second trail?",{"A":"It was easier for members with sore knees.","B":"It was shorter than the first trail.","C":"It had no views at all.","D":"The first trail was closed by rain."},"A","The passage says the second trail is mostly flat and directly gives sore knees as the reason for choosing it.","Combine the comparison with the explicit because reason; do not confuse shorter with easier for this group.",["Compare the trails: first is shorter and steep; second is longer and flat.","Locate the group condition: two members have sore knees.","Read the stated reason after because.","Reject shorter, no views, and closure claims not supported.","Choose A because flat terrain better fits the stated need."],"medium"),
make(6,"Read: 'The museum's new sign uses large letters and pictures. Visitors can understand the map even when the entrance is crowded.' What is the likely purpose of the sign design?",{"A":"To make directions easier to understand.","B":"To make the entrance more crowded.","C":"To replace every museum exhibit.","D":"To prevent visitors from seeing the map."},"A","Large letters and pictures help visitors understand the map, especially in a crowded entrance; A states the likely purpose.","Connect the design features with the benefit described in the second sentence.",["Identify the design features: large letters and pictures.","Identify the result: visitors understand the map.","Use even when crowded as evidence of accessibility.","Reject crowding, replacing exhibits, and blocking the map.","Choose A because it explains why the sign was designed that way."],"medium"),
make(7,"Read: 'Jin planned to walk home, but dark clouds gathered. He checked the weather app and called his father for a ride.' What can we infer about Jin?",{"A":"He changed his plan because he expected bad weather.","B":"He forgot where his home was.","C":"He wanted to walk in a storm.","D":"His father was already waiting at school."},"A","The contrast with dark clouds, weather check, and call for a ride supports the inference that Jin changed plans due to expected bad weather.","Use several connected clues instead of relying on one word: but, dark clouds, weather app, and ride.",["Record Jin's original plan: walk home.","Notice the change introduced by but.","Combine dark clouds and checking weather as risk clues.","Interpret calling for a ride as the new plan.","Choose A because it is the supported inference."],"hard"),
make(8,"Read: 'The student garden is not only a place to grow vegetables. It is also a quiet space where students observe insects, record weather, and share tasks.' Which title fits best?",{"A":"Learning Together in the Student Garden","B":"How to Close a Garden","C":"A Race to Buy Vegetables","D":"Why Students Avoid Outdoor Work"},"A","The passage presents the garden as a place for growing, observing, recording, and cooperation; A covers those activities.","Choose a title that includes the passage's broad purpose rather than one minor or opposite detail.",["List the activities: vegetables, insects, weather, and shared tasks.","Identify the common theme: learning and cooperation outdoors.","Compare that theme with each title.","Reject closing, buying, and avoiding work because they are not the focus.","Choose A because it captures the garden's educational use."],"medium"),
make(9,"Read: 'At first, the reading club had only four members. After students posted short reviews on the school website, twelve students joined the next month.' What caused the club to grow?",{"A":"The online reviews introduced the club to more students.","B":"The club stopped reading books.","C":"The school website closed.","D":"Four members left the school."},"A","The time order and After clause connect posting reviews with the increase from four to twelve members.","Trace the before-and-after change and identify the event immediately preceding the growth.",["Record the initial membership: four.","Find the event after which membership changes: reviews were posted.","Record the new membership: twelve.","Reject claims that deny or reverse the website event.","Select A because it gives the stated cause of growth."],"medium"),
make(10,"Read: 'Our class tested three ways to keep the room cool. Closing the blinds lowered the afternoon temperature most, while opening the windows helped only when the outside air was cooler. We will close the blinds first on hot days.' What conclusion did the class reach?",{"A":"Closing the blinds was the most reliable first action on hot days.","B":"Opening windows always made the room coldest.","C":"The class did not compare any methods.","D":"Hot days require keeping all windows closed forever."},"A","The test found closing blinds lowered temperature most, and the class explicitly chose it first; A keeps the conclusion within the tested context.","Integrate the result comparison with the class's stated action and avoid extending it beyond the evidence.",["Identify the three methods were compared.","Find the strongest result: closing blinds lowered temperature most.","Note the condition on windows: outside air must be cooler.","Read the stated plan for hot days.","Choose A because it combines evidence, action, and appropriate scope."],"hard"),
]
